# libtool -- packaged for libltdl, not for the libtool script.
#
# WHY IT IS HERE AT ALL. libcanberra's configure.ac 143-149 does
#
#     AC_CHECK_HEADER([ltdl.h], [AC_CHECK_LIB([ltdl], [lt_dladvise_init], ...)])
#     AS_IF([test "x$LIBLTDL" = "x"], [AC_MSG_ERROR([Unable to find libltdl.])])
#
# -- a hard configure failure. And it is not incidental: libcanberra is a thin
# core that dlopens its sound backends (libcanberra-alsa.so and friends), and
# libltdl is what performs the dlopen. There is no --disable-ltdl and no static
# path, so there is no libcanberra, and therefore no desktop event sounds,
# without this package.
#
# BLFS lists libcanberra's dependencies as libvorbis plus a few recommended ones
# and never mentions libtool -- because on a BLFS system it arrived in LFS
# chapter 8, hundreds of pages earlier. A dependency list can be silent because
# the book assumes its own earlier chapters, which is invisible from the page.
#
# WHY IT IS PINNED HERE AND NOT IN versions.env, EVEN THOUGH IT IS AN LFS
# PACKAGE. Exactly the reasoning pkgs/readline/pkg.env records, and readline is
# also an LFS chapter 8 package landed the same way: versions.env is generated
# ("do not edit") by tools/pin-versions.sh from a fixed PACKAGES array and is
# rewritten WHOLESALE on every run. Hand-adding LIBTOOL_* there contradicts the
# file's own header and would be destroyed by the next `make pin`; adding it to
# the PACKAGES array is the correct long-term home but only takes effect through
# a regeneration that re-downloads and re-hashes every LFS tarball in the tree --
# a change to every pin, landed in a pull request about desktop sound.
#
# README's "Versions" section already names openssl, cmake, ninja, go and rust
# as pinning in their own pkg.env for this shape of reason, and readline joined
# them today. This joins them too. The version is LFS 12.4's own 2.5.4, and its
# MD5 matches that book's md5sums file, so nothing here disagrees with it.
SRC_URL=https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/libtool/libtool-2.5.4.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=f81f5860666b0bc7d84baddefa60d1cb9fa6fceb2398cc3baca6afaa60266675
SRC_DIR=libtool-2.5.4

# --disable-static: nothing here links libltdl statically, and libcanberra
# dlopens through the shared one.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static"
